<title>SOUTH KOREA: Korea Heavy in $51 mln Taiwan boiler export deal.</title>
<headline>Korea Heavy in $51 mln Taiwan boiler export deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Korea Heavy Industries and Construction Co said on Thursday the company and ABB-CE of the United States had jointly won a $51 million contract from Taiwan's Formosa Plastics Group to build, operate and transfer four boilers for thermoelectric power plants.</p>
<p>The firm, owned by the South Korean government, will make and deliver the boilers for 600-megawatt plants by 1999, Korea Heavy said in a statement.</p>
<p>The statement gave no details on which roles ABB-CE will take in the deal or which terms will apply between the two companies.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5646</p>
</text>
